dexd (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Gapless HEVC video looper for Raspberry Pi, based on
    libmpv: dexd plays one video artwork in an endless loop with no visible
    break at the loop point.
  * The video, its sidecar and the exhibit config live together in /opt/dex.
    The exhibit config says which video plays, the display mode and the
    connector; the package installs none.
  * The sidecar binds the frame rate and a checksum to the video. Without it
    dexd refuses to start rather than guess the rate.
  * dexd checks the display mode, the boot options and the start of the video
    before it opens anything, and refuses with a message naming the fix.
  * While playing it checks that playback advances, recovers in place, writes
    a heartbeat to the system log, and lets the service manager restart it if
    it stops responding.
  * Commands on the player: dexd(1), dex-exhibit-apply(1), dex-wait-hdmi(1).
    The video is prepared on a workstation with dex-sidecar, which this package
    does not install.

 -- Max Albrecht <1@178.is>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
